  "query_preview": "..\nDrier southwesterlies are expected to continue across the Marianas\novernight, with another surge in the monsoon along with embedded\ndisturbances to more likely bring a peak in shower and thunder\ncoverage to the area around midweek. Conditions are expected to\nimprove considerably in the second half of the week, with only low-\nend scattered showers expected through at least Columbus Day.\nDeveloping Tropical Depression Koguma (27W) over the Marshall\nIslands, is not expected to bring any direct impacts to the Marianas\nat this time, but mariners may need to continue to monitor the\nsituation if any distant swells will arrive from the northeast by \nthe next weekend.",
